---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is dkim selector in simple terms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to memorize all of this?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does it take to implement?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What happens if I get it wrong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this the same across all DNS providers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Where can I get help if I'm stuck?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout title="What Is a DKIM Selector and How to Find Yours" description="DKIM selectors explained: how selector._domainkey naming works, where to find each provider's selector, and how to look the key up."  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DKIM Selectors</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">What Is a DKIM Selector?</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      A DKIM selector is the label that tells receivers <em>which</em> of your public keys to fetch.
      DKIM keys live at <code class="font-mono text-accent-soft">selector._domainkey.yourdomain.com</code>,
      and the selector in that name is chosen by whatever system signed the message.
    </p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>Why selectors exist</h2>
      <p>
        One domain usually sends through several systems: Google Workspace, an ESP, a billing
        service. Each publishes its own key, and selectors keep them from colliding:
        <code>google._domainkey</code> for Workspace, <code>s1._domainkey</code> for Zoho,
        <code>k1._domainkey</code> for Mailchimp. The message's DKIM-Signature header carries the
        selector, so the receiver knows exactly where to look. Multiple selectors also enable
        zero-downtime key rotation: publish the new selector alongside the old, switch signing,
        then retire the old one.
      </p>
      <h2>Common selectors by provider</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60">
        <table class="pdns-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Selector(s)</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="text-sm text-ink">Google Workspace</td><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">google</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="text-sm text-ink">Microsoft 365</td><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">selector1, selector2</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="text-sm text-ink">Mailchimp</td><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">k1, k2</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="text-sm text-ink">Zoho</td><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">s1, s2 (zoho)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="text-sm text-ink">SendGrid</td><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">smtpapi / custom (per-domain)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="text-sm text-ink">Postmark</td><td class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">custom per sending domain</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h2>How to find the one actually in use</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-5">
        <li>Send yourself a test message and open <em>show original / view source</em>.</li>
        <li>Find the <code>DKIM-Signature</code> header and read its <code>s=</code> tag: that is the selector.</li>
        <li>Plug domain + selector into the <a href="/dkim-record-checker/">DKIM checker</a> to verify the key resolves and its strength.</li>
      </ol>
      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is dkim selector in simple terms?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to memorize all of this?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take to implement?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens if I get it wrong?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is this the same across all DNS providers?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where can I get help if I'm stuck?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/dkim/">DKIM explained</a></li>
        <li><a href="/how-to-add-dkim-record/">How to add a DKIM record</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
